/li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link expandable\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p4\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"735\" data-source-start=\"717\">Accepting Your Aid</span></span></a><div class=\"slide\">\n<ul class=\"group level1\">\n<li class=\"item first\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p4_p0\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"755\" data-source-start=\"736\">Financial Aid Offer</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item last\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p4_p1\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"776\" data-source-start=\"756\">Financial Aid Portal</span></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link expandable\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p5\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"789\" data-source-start=\"777\">Types of Aid</span></span></a><div class=\"slide\">\n<ul class=\"group level1\">\n<li class=\"item first\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p5_p0\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"796\" data-source-start=\"790\">Grants</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p5_p1\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"809\" data-source-start=\"797\">Scholarships</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p5_p2\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"815\" data-source-start=\"810\">Loans</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p5_p3\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"853\" data-source-start=\"816\">Graduate Assistantships &amp; Fellowships</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item last\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p5_p4\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"877\" data-source-start=\"854\">Aggie Assurance Program</span></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link expandable\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p6\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"901\" data-source-start=\"878\">Maintaining Eligibility</span></span></a><div class=\"slide\">\n<ul class=\"group level1\">\n<li class=\"item first\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p6_p0\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"932\" data-source-start=\"902\">Satisfactory Academic Progress</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p6_p1\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"946\" data-source-start=\"933\">How to Appeal</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item last\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p6_p2\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"964\" data-source-start=\"947\">Enrollment Status</span></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p7\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"977\" data-source-start=\"965\">Scholarships</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link expandable\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p8\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"996\" data-source-start=\"978\">Student Employment</span></span></a><div class=\"slide\">\n<ul class=\"group level1\">\n<li class=\"item first\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p8_p0\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1032\" data-source-start=\"997\">Federal or Texas College Work Study</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p8_p1\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1052\" data-source-start=\"1033\">Part-Time Employent</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p8_p2\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1075\" data-source-start=\"1053\">Reads &amp; Counts Program</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p8_p3\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1101\" data-source-start=\"1076\">Community Service Program</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item last\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p8_p4\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1117\" data-source-start=\"1102\">Jobs for Aggies</span></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p9\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1126\" data-source-start=\"1118\">Veterans</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link expandable\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p10\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1143\" data-source-start=\"1127\">Parent Resources</span></span></a><div class=\"slide\">\n<ul class=\"group level1\">\n<li class=\"item first\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p10_p0\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1165\" data-source-start=\"1144\">Preparing for College</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item last\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p10_p1\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1184\" data-source-start=\"1166\">Saving for College</span></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p11\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1200\" data-source-start=\"1185\">Tax Information</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p12\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1204\" data-source-start=\"1201\">FAQ</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p13\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1232\" data-source-start=\"1205\">Prospective Student Centers</span></span></a></li><li class=\"item last\"><a class=\"link\" id=\"ctl00_cphLeftNavBar_ctl00_RadPanelbar1_p14\"><span class=\"text\"><span data-source-end=\"1248\" data-source-start=\"1233\">Code of Conduct</span></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td height=\"600px\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\" valign=\"top\" width=\"660px\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"10\" width=\"660px\"><tr><td>\n<p><span class=\"sfaheader\"><span data-source-end=\"1269\" data-source-start=\"1249\">TEXAS B-ON-TIME LOAN</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"1613\" data-source-start=\"1270\">The Texas B-On-Time Loan is a no-interest loan for eligible Texas students. This loan carries the added benefit that, if the borrower meets specified goals, the entire loan amount can be forgiven upon graduation. This loan is funded by the State of Texas, with repayment made to Hinson Hazelwood, the Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"sfasubheader\"><span data-source-end=\"1625\" data-source-start=\"1614\">Eligibility</span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"1687\" data-source-start=\"1626\">You must be a renewal student (previously awarded B-On-Time).</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"1727\" data-source-start=\"1688\">You must be within 150 attempted hours.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"1764\" data-source-start=\"1728\">You must maintain a minimum 2.5 GPA.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"1822\" data-source-start=\"1765\">You must complete 75% of previous year’s attempted hours.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"1852\" data-source-start=\"1823\">You must be a Texas resident.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2085\" data-source-start=\"1853\">You must have graduated from a public or accredited private high school in Texas during or after the 2002-2003 academic year. Or, you must have received an associate’s degree from an eligible institution no earlier than May 1, 2005.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2269\" data-source-start=\"2086\">If not a resident, you must not have graduated from a high school prior to May 2003, and you must be the dependent of military personnel who is entitled to pay resident tuition rates.</span></span> </li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2345\" data-source-start=\"2270\">You must have completed the recommended or advanced high school curriculum.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2391\" data-source-start=\"2346\">You must have not earned a bachelor's degree.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2500\" data-source-start=\"2392\">You must be enrolled full-time in an undergraduate degree or certificate program at an eligible institution.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2584\" data-source-start=\"2501\">You must have completed the FAFSA and be eligible to receive federal financial aid.</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2684\" data-source-start=\"2585\">You must have been certified by the designated school as eligible for Texas B-On-Time Student Loan.</span></span> </li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class=\"sfasubheader\"><span data-source-end=\"2717\" data-source-start=\"2685\">Hardships or Other Proper Causes</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"2792\" data-source-start=\"2718\">You have the right to submit an appeal to receive your B-On-Time Loan. The</span> <leo_highlight id=\"leoHighlights_Underline_0\" style=\"border-bottom: rgb(255,255,150) 2px solid; display: inline; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; cursor: pointer; -moz-background-size: auto auto; -moz-background-clip: -moz-initial; -moz-background-origin: -moz-initial; -moz-background-inline-policy: -moz-initial\"></leo_highlight><span data-source-end=\"2865\" data-source-start=\"2793\">request must be submitted in writing and must explain the reason for the</span> <leo_highlight id=\"leoHighlights_Underline_1\" style=\"border-bottom: rgb(255,255,150) 2px solid; display: inline; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; cursor: pointer; -moz-background-size: auto auto; -moz-background-clip: -moz-initial; -moz-background-origin: -moz-initial; -moz-background-inline-policy: -moz-initial\"></leo_highlight><span data-source-end=\"2914\" data-source-start=\"2866\">request. Reasons that may be considered include:</span></span> </p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"3014\" data-source-start=\"2915\">A showing of a severe illness or other debilitating condition that may affect academic performance;</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"3171\" data-source-start=\"3015\">An indication that you are responsible for the care of a sick, injured, or needy person and that your provision of care may affect academic performance; and</span> </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"3237\" data-source-start=\"3172\">That you require less than 12 hours to complete your degree plan.</span></span> </li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"3298\" data-source-start=\"3238\">A financial aid advisor or administrator will respond to the</span> <leo_highlight id=\"leoHighlights_Underline_2\" style=\"border-bottom: rgb(255,255,150) 2px solid; display: inline; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; cursor: pointer; -moz-background-size: auto auto; -moz-background-clip: -moz-initial; -moz-background-origin: -moz-initial; -moz-background-inline-policy: -moz-initial\"></leo_highlight><span data-source-end=\"3503\" data-source-start=\"3299\">request through your NEO email account or regular mail. A copy of all correspondence will be placed in your financial aid file. Submitting an appeal does not guarantee any adjustments can or will be made.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"QuickLinks\"><span data-source-end=\"3597\" data-source-start=\"3504\">For more information about your eligibility for the loan and forgiveness requirements, please</span> <a><span data-source-end=\"3608\" data-source-start=\"3598\">click here</span></a><span data-source-end=\"3610\" data-source-start=\"3609\">.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"sfabody\"><span data-source-end=\"3682\" data-source-start=\"3611\">Forgiven B-On-Time loans must be reported to the IRS as taxable income.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"QuickLinks\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"sfacategory\"><span data-source-end=\"3823\" data-source-start=\"3683\">NOTE: There is not a separate application for the B-On-Time Loan. Eligibility is based on the FAFSA and availability of institutional funds.</span></span> </p>\n\n</td></tr></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div id=\"accentbar\">\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"28px\" style=\"background-color:#000000;\" width=\"100%\">   </td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div id=\"footer\">\n<table width=\"910px\">\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"20%\">\n<span class=\"footertext\" style=\"font-family: arial\"><span data-source-end=\"3852\" data-source-start=\"3824\">Scholarships &amp; Financial Aid</span><br/>\r\n<span data-source-end=\"3884\" data-source-start=\"3853\">The Pavilion 200, Spence Street</span><br/>\r\n<span data-source-end=\"3894\" data-source-start=\"3885\">1252 TAMU</span><br/>\r\n<span data-source-end=\"3925\" data-source-start=\"3895\">College Station, TX 77843-1252</span></span><br/>\n<br/>\n<span class=\"footertext\" style=\"font-family: arial\"><span data-source-end=\"3945\" data-source-start=\"3926\">Hours of operation:</span><br/>\r\n<span data-source-end=\"3978\" data-source-start=\"3946\">Monday - Friday (8am to 5pm CST)</span></span>\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"60%\">\n<center>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"5\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a><span>FAQs - Aggie Answers</span></a></td>\n<td>\n<div class=\"faq_askag1\"><span data-source-end=\"4014\" data-source-start=\"3979\">Can't find what you're looking for?</span><br/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"faq_askag2\"><span data-source-end=\"4018\" data-source-start=\"4015\">Ask</span><br/>\r\n            <span data-source-end=\"4032\" data-source-start=\"4019\">Aggie Answers</span></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\">  </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</center>\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"20%\">\n<p class=\"rtfootertext\"><span data-source-end=\"4064\" data-source-start=\"4033\">© 2009-2011 All rights reserved</span></p>\n<br/>\n<p class=\"rtfootertext\"><span data-source-end=\"4085\" data-source-start=\"4065\">Texas A&amp;M University</span></p>\n<br/>\n<p class=\"rtfootertext\"><span data-source-end=\"4114\" data-source-start=\"4086\">College Station, Texas 77843</span> </p>\n<p align=\"right\" class=\"rtfootertext\"><a><span data-source-end=\"4153\" data-source-start=\"4115\">Texas A&amp;M University Privacy Statement</span></a></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n<div id=\"postpage\">\n<center>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"910\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" class=\"BottomLinks\"><a><span data-source-end=\"4168\" data-source-start=\"4154\">State of Texas</span></a> <span data-source-end=\"4170\" data-source-start=\"4169\">|</span> <a><span data-source-end=\"4194\" data-source-start=\"4171\">Texas Homeland Security</span></a> <span data-source-end=\"4196\" data-source-start=\"4195\">|</span> <a><span data-source-end=\"4209\" data-source-start=\"4197\">Open Records</span></a> <span data-source-end=\"4211\" data-source-start=\"4210\">|</span> <a><span data-source-end=\"4254\" data-source-start=\"4212\">Texas A&amp;M System Risk &amp; Misconduct Hotline</span></a> <span data-source-end=\"4256\" data-source-start=\"4255\">|</span> <a><span data-source-end=\"4274\" data-source-start=\"4257\">State Wide Search</span></a> <span data-source-end=\"4276\" data-source-start=\"4275\">|</span> <a><span data-source-end=\"4294\" data-source-start=\"4277\">State Link Policy</span></a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" class=\"BottomText\"><span data-source-end=\"4351\" data-source-start=\"4295\">Texas A&amp;M is a member of the Texas A&amp;M University System</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</center>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n", "text": "Financial Aid Home | Calendar | Forms | Contact Us | TAMU | Aggie Answers PROSPECTIVE STUDENTS | CURRENT STUDENTS | GRADUATE | INTERNATIONAL | STUDENT ATHLETES Financial Aid Basics Determining Financial Need College Cost Calculator Dependency Status Extenuating Circumstances Non-Degree Seeking Student Withdrawing from the University Glossary Cost of Attendance Undergraduate Students Graduate Students MBA Students Veterinary Students How to Apply Free Application for Federal Student Aid Texas Application for State Financial Aid (SB 1528) International Student Financial Aid Application Summer Supplement Processing Your Aid Estimated Family Contribution Student Aid Report Verification Quality Assurance Program Accepting Your Aid Financial Aid Offer Financial Aid Portal Types of Aid Grants Scholarships Loans Graduate Assistantships & Fellowships Aggie Assurance Program Maintaining Eligibility Satisfactory Academic Progress How to Appeal Enrollment Status Scholarships Student Employment Federal or Texas College Work Study Part-Time Employent Reads & Counts Program Community Service Program Jobs for Aggies Veterans Parent Resources Preparing for College Saving for College Tax Information FAQ Prospective Student Centers Code of Conduct TEXAS B-ON-TIME LOAN The Texas B-On-Time Loan is a no-interest loan for eligible Texas students. This loan carries the added benefit that, if the borrower meets specified goals, the entire loan amount can be forgiven upon graduation. This loan is funded by the State of Texas, with repayment made to Hinson Hazelwood, the Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board. Eligibility You must be a renewal student (previously awarded B-On-Time). You must be within 150 attempted hours. You must maintain a minimum 2.5 GPA. You must complete 75% of previous year’s attempted hours. You must be a Texas resident. You must have graduated from a public or accredited private high school in Texas during or after the 2002-2003 academic year. Or, you must have received an associate’s degree from an eligible institution no earlier than May 1, 2005. If not a resident, you must not have graduated from a high school prior to May 2003, and you must be the dependent of military personnel who is entitled to pay resident tuition rates. You must have completed the recommended or advanced high school curriculum. You must have not earned a bachelor's degree. You must be enrolled full-time in an undergraduate degree or certificate program at an eligible institution. You must have completed the FAFSA and be eligible to receive federal financial aid. You must have been certified by the designated school as eligible for Texas B-On-Time Student Loan. Hardships or Other Proper Causes You have the right to submit an appeal to receive your B-On-Time Loan. The request must be submitted in writing and must explain the reason for the request. Reasons that may be considered include: A showing of a severe illness or other debilitating condition that may affect academic performance; An indication that you are responsible for the care of a sick, injured, or needy person and that your provision of care may affect academic performance; and That you require less than 12 hours to complete your degree plan. A financial aid advisor or administrator will respond to the request through your NEO email account or regular mail. A copy of all correspondence will be placed in your financial aid file. Submitting an appeal does not guarantee any adjustments can or will be made. For more information about your eligibility for the loan and forgiveness requirements, please click here . Forgiven B-On-Time loans must be reported to the IRS as taxable income. NOTE: There is not a separate application for the B-On-Time Loan. Eligibility is based on the FAFSA and availability of institutional funds. Scholarships & Financial Aid The Pavilion 200, Spence Street 1252 TAMU College Station, TX 77843-1252 Hours of operation: Monday - Friday (8am to 5pm CST) Can't find what you're looking for? Ask Aggie Answers © 2009-2011 All rights reserved Texas A&M University College Station, Texas 77843 Texas A&M University Privacy Statement State of Texas | Texas Homeland Security | Open Records | Texas A&M System Risk & Misconduct Hotline | State Wide Search | State Link Policy Texas A&M is a member of the Texas A&M University System", "source_sha256": "e0324811d23de850ba827ac84e9e6c303b166bf870ae0f6010210c7ebf0e0eeb", "retained_assets": 0, "omitted_assets": 17}